# How we work (Idle Party)

Source: the owner, who vibe-codes. Last sync: **2026-10-09**.
Order when rules disagree: `00-locks` → `10-what-to-build` → this file →
`30-done`. Growth principles: `docs/GROWTH_MANDATE.md`.

**Now:** the agent picks and builds the next batch from checked facts (10-what-to-build). A goal the owner names wins. **Never Play AAB without owner ask.**

## Talking to the owner

- They give everyday goals. They do not name APIs, files, or skills.
- Talk in plain, short Swedish (or their language). If a technical word is
  needed, add one plain synonym. In-game text stays English.
- Pick skills, tools, tests, and commands yourself. Follow the project skill
  whose description matches the task. Do not ask "ska jag använda X?" or how
  to code it.
- Do not explain which tools you used unless they ask "hur gjorde du?".
- For a product, risk, or design fork, read `decide-a-fork` quietly and make
  one decision. If unclear whether they mean menus or combat ("two different
  games"), the Executive Producer decides. No chair vote. Prefer shipping
  something playable.

## What to work on

No goal, or a vague one: pick one batch from the evidence in
`10-what-to-build.mdc` and build it. Do not ask what to do. Do not invent a
numbered program.

"Mer endgame" with no new content named: deepen KEY, Gauntlet, Rift,
Greater Rift, and Ashen. The monthly Craft Trial (MORE → CRAFT) is not a
sixth ENDGAME hunt.

Do not run `/init` or clean up the repo unless they ask. Change GEAR or
endgame copy only when play notes say it lies.

Play notes usually come from a new save. Write each note into
`docs/PLAY_NOTES.md` under Open when the owner gives it, and move it to Done
with the commit that fixes it. Read Open at the start of a batch.

## UI and distribution (facts)

- Phones are about 360–430 CSS px wide. The reference is the Samsung A56
  at 360×780.
- The live look is the AVD `Samsung_A56` with `flutter run`
  (`a56-playtest`). Not Pixel_6, and not stacked web-server tabs.
- Web is only a fallback through Playwright / `WebClickBridge` (forced
  360×780).
- The Play package is `com.idleparty.app`.
- Testers never get a build before the owner.

## Work loop

1. Work in large batches you can finish alone.
2. Before handoff, verify with `30-done`: analyze plus the matching tests,
   and hub smoke or the A56 if UI changed. After kit number changes,
   share-fast and the balance gate must be green.
3. If the owner should look at the phone, push this batch to the A56 first
   (`a56-playtest`, hot restart or relaunch). Do not ask them to look while
   the emulator still runs a session from before the edits.
4. Before a big change to look or feel (sizes, speeds, or the layout of a
   whole screen or floor), show the owner a before and an after on the A56
   and let them pick. Then build on the pick. Small tweaks need no preview.
5. Hand off in at most 5 lines: what you chose and the source, what changed,
   and a short test list for a new save. Add an endgame save only if endgame
   changed. Then wait.
6. **Git:** when analyze and tests are green, **commit locally** without
   asking. Push, open a PR, or tag when the batch needs it, also without
   asking. **Never upload an AAB to Google Play unless the owner asks in
   that turn.** Never force-push or use `--no-verify` unless they say so in
   that turn. This **overrides** any global "only commit when asked" rule
   for this repo.
7. Daily work goes on `main`. Use `release/*` only when cutting a tag.
8. Do not stage `windows/flutter/generated_*` unless plugins actually
   changed.
9. When a change needs a home, split the giant file. Do not grow
   `game_logic`, `spatial_combat`, or fat shells. New HUD goes under
   `lib/ui/shell/`.
10. Delete unused code that saves do not need. Keep JSON fields that old
   saves may still have.

## Decide alone / Never

| Decide alone | Never |
|--------------|--------|
| Skills, files, analyze/tests, splits, dead non-save code | Weaken Legal / IP or Cursor safety |
| The next batch, from the evidence in `10-what-to-build.mdc` | Invent a numbered program they did not ask for |
| New zone / class / hunt / God Hand direction / scaled UA / IAP, a second sim, or gacha when they name it, or when an A source and a hole in this game agree | |
| Commit, push, PR, tag when green | Force-push; skip hooks; point players at GitHub Releases; **upload Play AAB without owner ask** |
| A56 look / hub smoke; listing docs; wipe test save if needed; Console paste | |

Ask the owner only when this table does not let you decide.

## Feel reminders

- Keep the hub readable and calm when you can.
- Fairness: if a kit is fun but rated HIGH, trim its numbers. Its identity
  can stay.
